    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe torch indexer of DeepSeek-V4.1 (the path GPUs without DeepGEMM's paged MQA logits take, e.g. SM12x) scores a prefill in chunks of a bf16 `[rows, 64 heads, keys]` product capped at `_TORCH_SCORE_BUDGET_BYTES` (1 GiB). `scores()` then did `(s.relu() * weights.unsqueeze(-1)).sum(dim=1)`: `relu()` and the multiply each allocated another tensor of the chunk's size, so a chunk peaked at 3 GiB. On 12-16 GB cards that is the largest transient of a long prefill, and it is where the prefill runs out of memory.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `dsv41_sparse.py`, `DeepseekV41Indexer.scores()`: `relu_()` and `mul_()` on the einsum's own output, then the same `sum(dim=1).float()`. The einsum returns a fresh tensor and `scores()` has one caller (`_score_chunks`), so nothing else sees it.\n- `v41_indexer/scoring.py`: the budget's comment no longer says transients run ~3x the cap.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nSame operations in the same order. On an RTX 5070 Ti (SM120), random bf16 inputs at four chunk shapes (rows x keys = 256 x 32768, 1024 x 8192, 4096 x 2048, 128 x 65536; 64 heads, d = 128): `torch.equal` between the old and new outputs at every shape.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nSame shapes, 20 calls each after warm-up (`torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated` above the inputs):\n\n| | time a call | peak |\n|---|---|---|\n| out of place (before) | 9.0-9.1 ms | 3072 MiB |\n| in place (this PR) | 9.2-9.3 ms | 1072 MiB |\n\nIn a server (2x RTX 5070 Ti 16 GB, TP2, KTransformers CPU experts, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017): before this change, with 12 GB of each card usable an 11.8K-token prompt ran out of memory allocating 1 GiB in `scores()`, and with 16 GB a second 35K-token prompt (four 9,216-token chunks) did the same after the first had passed; with it, both prompts pass. The 35K prefill's speed is unchanged within launch noise (675 / 663 tok/s with the change, 678 / 671 without).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39728379906](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39728379906)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39728379461](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39728379461)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39728379532](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39728379532)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
